From 6c2061016881f8b367ad72e7599c850b30d91fd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "cline-cloud[bot]" <cline-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(render): retire the self-hosted deploy path and name
 Render everywhere

jp-agent deploys from git to Render (project/decisions.md D-14), so nothing
should deploy to a droplet again.

* deploy-droplet.yml is deleted. It targeted runs-on [self-hosted,
  jp-agent-droplet], a label the runner never carried, so no run of it ever
  succeeded -- every one queued until it was cancelled. Nothing that worked is
  lost with it.
* ci-cd.yml keeps its jp-agent job (it runs on ubuntu-latest); only the name and
  the rationale comment referenced the droplet, and they now name Render and
  render.yaml.
* actionlint.yaml drops the four self-hosted labels: no self-hosted runs-on is
  left, so the list is dead config, and the note says how to restore it.

This identity has no `workflows` permission (GitHub rejects the push with
"refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow"), so the change
ships as project/reports/2026-10-19-retire-jp-agent-droplet.patch.
